config TIMER_RISCITRY
	bool "RISCitry machine timer"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_RISCITRY_TIMER_ENABLED
	select TICKLESS_CAPABLE
	select TIMER_HAS_64BIT_CYCLE_COUNTER
	help
	  System clock on the RISCitry mtime/mtimecmp (source/computer/timer.luc). Same registers as
	  the generic RISC-V machine timer, but all divides and multiplies are 32-bit: the upstream
	  driver pulls in libgcc's 64-bit divide (1.6 KB), which matters in a 16 KB RAM that holds code
	  and data. Tickless only.
